verdicts={"353624054":("REFUTED",False,"Positive off-target eclipse deficit: Gaussian source 1.540 pixels from target, 0.126 pixels from plausible contaminant Gaia 2005581162670064512 (G13.526). Its 7.667069-d eclipse train is unrelated to the selected 34.896-d Gaia clock. Target eclipsing interpretation is refuted; the contaminating binary is not claimed as a new by-catch.","Confirm exact contaminant identity with higher resolution if scientifically useful."),"355095704":("CONFIRMED",True,"Three resolved narrow eclipses in sectors 1,27,95, with a coherent 43.301407-d clock. Target-centered deficit offset 0.197 pixel and a same-photon custom aperture independently retains the eclipse; no capable Gaia neighbor within the bounded six-pixel audit. Source-specific Gaia conjunction residuals 0.86-2.13d are comparable to propagated 0.80-2.31d errors; period differs 0.82 nominal Gaia sigma.","Further events can improve timing precision."),"357128110":("CONFIRMED",True,"Deep flat-bottomed eclipses recur in sectors82,84,86 at 58.239278d. Difference Gaussian is 0.039 pixel from target; custom aperture retains 137ppt eclipse. A capable distant Gaia neighbor is 5.86pixels away and inconsistent with centered source. Gaia period differs 1.04 sigma; conjunction displacement10.7d remains compatible with large propagated9.2d covariance uncertainty.","Further cycles and spectroscopy can refine orbital association."),"371308305":("REFUTED",False,"Repeated narrow eclipses have a coherent 1.408705-d clock, incompatible with the selected43.570-d Gaia orbit. Difference Gaussian lies1.423pixels from target and0.135pixel from Gaia2003601698136576640 (G15.476), with another close faint source nearby. This is positive off-target evidence; exact contaminant identity remains bounded and no by-catch is counted.","Resolve which faint neighbor owns the eclipse if useful."),"381290484":("CONFIRMED",True,"Raw primary eclipses in sectors39,66,93 give52.648523d; opposite-conjunction eclipses in100,102 independently give52.647048d from same-kind midpoints. The latter rejects primary half-period and sparse integer aliases through actual covered nulls. Difference image in100 is0.106pixel from target and custom aperture retains66ppt. Capable neighbors at2.82 and4.11pixels are spatially inconsistent. Gaia period differs1.26sigma and covariance conjunction offsets0.59-1.58d remain near1.1-1.3 nominal sigma.","Joint characterization may refine the two conjunction shapes and ephemeris."),"418062110":("PROBABLE",True,"Deep flat eclipses in sectors91,92 recur26.073508d apart. Covered predicted half-period/divisor repeats are absent; the representative source deficit is0.068pixel from target with143ppt custom-aperture loss, inconsistent with capable neighbors at>=2.59pixels. A shallow opposite eclipse is also visible in92. Repeated eclipses are robust; final physical tier is PROBABLE because Gaia-orbit association remains uncertain because photometric period differs3.71 nominal Gaia sigma and deep conjunction offset~5.5d is1.8 propagated sigma. The missing Gaia-compatible geometry check prevents CONFIRMED under Section2.7.","Obtain another deep eclipse and update spectroscopy to resolve Gaia period tension."),"437230472":("PLAUSIBLE",False,"S9 andS100 contain genuine broad flat-bottomed losses, whileS63 is a step andS90 is sloped variability, excluded from eclipse timings. FreshS100 custom aperture retains47ppt and is0.082pixel from target. Two events2524.782d apart leave many tested integer-cycle alternatives;47.637395d is a conditional53-cycle example, not a resolved period. It differs strongly from47.189d Gaia orbit. Physical recurrence/association is unresolved despite credible morphology; not counted.","Find a third same-kind eclipse to resolve integer aliases and Gaia association."),"442807330":("PROBABLE",False,"Repeated resolved eclipses show2.315273d spacing and a robust same-photon alternative aperture. Source ownership is unresolved because known EB TIC442802434/Gaia5863330614835332608 (G13.148) lies4.927arcsec away, only0.24pixel, and is capable. Broad target-centered deficit cannot distinguish those sources. Mandatory known-neighbor ownership and novelty hold; no addition. Selected25.662d Gaia association is not established.","Resolve target from the known capable EB with higher resolution and compare its published clock.")}
