 text=f"# {r['sample_id']}: TIC {tic} / Gaia DR3 {r['gaia_dr3']}\n\nPhysical tier: **{tier}**. Bounded review: **complete**. Addition eligibility: **{eligible}**, subject to root acceptance and sealed catalogue reconciliation.\n\n{reason}\n\nRepresentative raw events: {len(context['flag_events'])} screen windows inspected across {len(context['source'])} QLP files. The raw SAP morphology image and numeric series are retained. Quality==0, finite positive flux is used; gaps and unsuitable windows do not count as clean nulls. KSPSAP is plotted when available but can suppress broad eclipses.\n\nTiming summary: conditional selected clock {p:.9f} d, epoch {c['epoch_btjd']:.7f} BTJD, local formal period error {perr:.3g} d, residual maximum {c['max_residual_d']:.5f} d. Error floors per midpoint: cadence/2 and0.002d. These are local fit errors and cycle-conditional, not posterior precision or guaranteed prediction errors. Duration {c['duration_d']:.4f}d and depth {c['depth_ppt']:.2f}ppt are selected raw-fit descriptors. For437 the period/error are explicitly unresolved-alias descriptors. Distinct conjunction kinds are never counted as same-kind repeats.\n\nCoverage audit: selected measured clock has {a[0]['covered']} actually usable predicted windows and {len(a[0]['nulls'])} clean nulls. Divisors2..6 and all first-to-last integer alternatives over5..100d (0.6..100d for short clocks) are tested against same-kind timing tolerance0.04d and covered windows. Core coverage>=75%, at least3 core/side samples, gap limit max(3cadence,0.2duration); null threshold max(15% selected depth,4noise/sqrt(N)). Timing-incompatible alternatives are excluded before flux evaluation; missing/flagged coverage is unknown. Full tests retained.\n\nAttribution/alternative reduction: custom7x7 TESScut data, core inside0.25duration and sidebands0.75-2duration, background-subtracted3x3 aperture. This reuses TESS photons; it is a reduction check, not an independent observation. Positive-deficit centroids and Gaussian fits are descriptive, not calibrated exclusion radii. Neighbor G-flux capability estimates are approximate TESS proxies; required intrinsic neighbor loss is not compared directly with blended pixel loss. Source-specific spatial evidence determines attribution.\n\nGaia geometry: source-specific SB1 linear covariance propagated with fixed local cycle and edge-on conjunction assumptions. Mass function {g.get('mass_function_solar',float('nan')):.5f} solar masses; e={g.get('eccentricity',float('nan')):.4f}. Long resolved durations and stellar-eclipse depths are physically plausible where morphology is accepted. Gaia association is separate from physical eclipse classification; no inclination or full posterior is claimed.\n\nCatalogue: uses sealed second/shared-catalogues receipts (VSX, ASAS-SN, vetted EB tables, Gaia, SIMBAD, Kepler/TOI bounded checks) retained in lead-central-catalogue-receipts.json. Successful scoped nonmatches are not exhaustive novelty proof; failures remain unknown. Known-neighbor hold explicitly overrides addition eligibility for442807330.\n\nLimitations/next check: {nextcheck} Representative bounded review is not exhaustive all-event/all-sector characterization. Lead visually inspected all eight raw-context panels and deciding localization panels, plus437 freshS100. Helper audit is retained separately when available. Source FITS hashes validated against frozen parent population and TIC/sector headers, exact nested Gaia G/identity verified. Scripts, measurements, images and receipts are sealed in final manifest; no ledger or public files edited.\n"
